{"ts": 1793468650.796, "kind": "tool_start", "step": 6, "tool": "edit_file", "blast": "write", "args": {"new_string": "## Findings\n- Bug reproduced (sympy @ e8c22f6eac): `SI._collect_factor_and_dimension(a1*t1 + v1)` raises `ValueError: Dimension of \"v1\" is Dimension(velocity), but it should be Dimension(acceleration*time)`. a1*t1 → (-49.0, Dimension(acceleration*time)), v1 → (2, Dimension(velocity)) — equivalent dims, structurally different.\n- Cause: `sympy/physics/units/unitsystem.py` Add branch (line ~178) compares dims with strict `dim != addend_dim` instead of dimensional equivalence.\n- Available machinery: `DimensionSystem.equivalent_dims(dim1, dim2)` in sympy/physics/units/dimensions.py:428 compares `get_dimensional_dependencies` dicts.\n\n## Leads\n- Minimal fix: in Add branch, when `dim != addend_dim`, fall back to `self.get_dimension_system().equivalent_dims(dim, addend_dim)`; if equivalent, continue (adopt addend_dim) else raise.\n\n## Questions\n- Which exact dim to keep when equivalent (first vs addend) — check existing tests in sympy/physics/units/tests/test_unitsystem.py for expected return dims.\n\n## Decisions\n- Fix goes in source only (unitsystem.py); no test edits, no commit (per TASK.md).", "old_string": "## Findings\n## Leads\n## Questions\n## Decisions", "path": "notes.md"}}
{"seq": 40, "ts": 1793468650.797, "kind": "tool_start", "step": 6, "tool": "edit_file", "blast": "write", "args": {"new_string": "## Findings\n- Bug reproduced (sympy @ e8c22f6eac): `SI._collect_factor_and_dimension(a1*t1 + v1)` raises `ValueError: Dimension of \"v1\" is Dimension(velocity), but it should be Dimension(acceleration*time)`. a1*t1 → (-49.0, Dimension(acceleration*time)), v1 → (2, Dimension(velocity)) — equivalent dims, structurally different.\n- Cause: `sympy/physics/units/unitsystem.py` Add branch (line ~178) compares dims with strict `dim != addend_dim` instead of dimensional equivalence.\n- Available machinery: `DimensionSystem.equivalent_dims(dim1, dim2)` in sympy/physics/units/dimensions.py:428 compares `get_dimensional_dependencies` dicts.\n\n## Leads\n- Minimal fix: in Add branch, when `dim != addend_dim`, fall back to `self.get_dimension_system().equivalent_dims(dim, addend_dim)`; if equivalent, continue (adopt addend_dim) else raise.\n\n## Questions\n- Which exact dim to keep when equivalent (first vs addend) — check existing tests in sympy/physics/units/tests/test_unitsystem.py for expected return dims.\n\n## Decisions\n- Fix goes in source only (unitsystem.py); no test edits, no commit (per TASK.md).", "old_string": "## Findings\n## Leads\n## Questions\n## Decisions", "path": "notes.md"}}
